  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The conductor may change phrasing or dynamics; an agreed change record lists the piece, bar number, and current marking.\", \"decision\": \"How should changes to score markings be kept consistent?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nSingers mark changes during rehearsal, and the conductor reviews the affected bars aloud before the organizer publishes the change record. Immediate personal notes are followed by a common confirmation that can correct misheard instructions before everyone leaves.\nSection leaders note changed markings during rehearsal and compare their notes with the conductor before updating the shared record. A brief check catches differences between sections before the final instructions are circulated to the whole choir.\nThe conductor announces each changed marking, and the organizer enters it in the shared change record during rehearsal. A central account is created as decisions occur, giving absent members and uncertain singers the same reference afterward."
    }
  ],
